# Edge (`apps/edge`)

Public deploy only. Locally the app is still Compose (`web` + `api`).

- `wrangler.jsonc`: Worker `thepower-kanban`, custom domain
  `thepower-kanban.josenuevo.dev` (zone in the same account). Assets from
  `../web/dist` with `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` and
  `run_worker_first: ["/api/*"]`.
- `src/index.ts`: `/api/*` → `getContainer(env.API, "main").fetch(request)`.
  Use `fetch`, never `containerFetch` (RPC; it breaks the WebSocket
  upgrade). Everything else → `env.ASSETS.fetch(request)`.
- `ApiContainer extends Container<Env>`: `defaultPort = 3000`,
  `sleepAfter = "4h"`, `envVars` from the Worker secrets
  (`BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`) plus
  `DATABASE_URL=file:/data/agentic-kanban.db` and `API_PORT=3000`.
  Durable Object binding `API`, migration `new_sqlite_classes`,
  `max_instances: 1`, `instance_type: "basic"`. Always the `"main"`
  instance: the board hub is in memory, so every user must reach the same
  process.
- `Dockerfile` (build context = repo root via `image_build_context: "../.."`):
  Bun 1.4.3, copies every workspace manifest, then
  `bun install --frozen-lockfile --filter` for api, db and schemas. No
  `--hot`, no bind mount. CMD runs `db:migrate`, `db:seed`, then the API as
  user `bun`. The Containers disk is ephemeral: each start begins from the
  seed and changes are lost when the container sleeps. Do not add another
  database.
- `worker-configuration.d.ts` comes from `wrangler types` (run inside
  `apps/edge`, `bun run types`) after any `wrangler.jsonc` change. It is
  excluded from fmt; do not edit it by hand.
- Secrets: only in the ignored `.env.cloudflare.local`, passed with
  `--secrets-file` by `bun run deploy:cloudflare`. Never print it, commit
  it, bake it into the image, or expose it to `apps/web`. `.dockerignore`
  excludes `.env`, `.env.*`, `*.local` and all of `data/`.
- Before deploying: `bunx wrangler whoami` shows the course account and
  Docker is running. Never use other projects' credentials. The first
  deploy needs a few minutes for the certificate and container.
